1	// dqi_ambient.rs — de-interlacing in the four-valued Belnap ambient 𝟒={N,T,F,B}
2	//
3	// The correction folded in from the principal's message: D₂ must act on
4	// 𝟒^{2m} BEFORE any Boolean/numerical retraction. The previous stride-2
5	// analysis studied R∘D₂ — collapse first, then de-interlace — which is one
6	// Boolean retraction too late. The primitive object is D₂ itself, then the
7	// DQI-conjugate J(a,b)=(a,¬b), and only after a component is structurally
8	// separable do we apply one of the two Boolean retractions r, c.
9	//
10	// Carrier: B₄={F,T} ⊊ 𝟒={N,T,F,B}, with N and B genuine ambient states.
11	// Two distinct collapses: r(N)=r(B)=T, c(N)=c(B)=F (belnap::r, belnap::c).
12	// Belnap negation: ¬T=F, ¬F=T, ¬N=N, ¬B=B (belnap::bnot).
13	// Therefore r∘¬ ≠ ¬∘r and c∘¬ ≠ ¬∘c exactly outside the Boolean core —
14	// verified exhaustively below (only four values, so exhaustive is a real
15	// claim, not a sampling one).
16	//
17	// Inc(B)=B (belnap::inc) has no Boolean factorization: r∘Inc and c∘Inc are
18	// constant T and F respectively, neither recovers B (corollary_11_2_report).
19	// So the ambient genuinely contains operations the Boolean core cannot host.
